tasks.task:
In lib/ChordPro/res/templates/html5/css/chord-diagrams.tt, add:
  (a) .cp-song-layout-right .cp-chord-diagrams { flex-direction: column; } — default for right panel
  (b) .cp-chord-diagrams-direction-vertical { flex-direction: column; }
  (c) .cp-chord-diagrams-direction-horizontal { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  These apply to both standard and paged HTML5 (paged content.tt includes chord-diagrams.tt directly).

In lib/ChordPro/Output/HTML5.pm render_chord_diagrams(), after reading $html5_diagrams:
  Read direction: my $direction = lc(eval { $html5_diagrams->{direction} } // '');
  Validate: $direction = '' unless $direction =~ /^(?:vertical|horizontal)\z/;
  Pass diagrams_direction => $direction to _process_template('chord_diagrams', ...).

In lib/ChordPro/res/config/chordpro.json, inside the html5 { } block, add:
  diagrams {
      // Layout direction for the chord diagram box when diagrams.show is "right".
      // Values: "vertical" (stacked, default) or "horizontal" (side-by-side).
      direction : "vertical"
  }
  Ensure the key is valid JSON5/relaxed JSON.
